// `null_ptr<T>()` AS A FIELD DEFAULT — the one call a default may make.
//
// A default is written at EVERY construction that omitted the field, so
// `gen_c_const.is_pure_value` admits only what can be written twice
// without anyone being able to tell: literals, operators over them, and
// constructions. A call is none of those and is refused — see
// tests/must-fail/codegen/field_default_that_calls_a_function.zen.
//
// `null_ptr<T>()` is spelled like a call and is not one. `mem_ptr.zen`
// gives it no body ("a function, not a constant: a constant would still
// need a T, and the call site always has one"); `gen_c_ptr.zen` IS its
// body, and what that body writes is `((T *)NULL)` — a constant naming
// nothing and reading nothing. So it is admitted, and admitted for that
// reason rather than by its spelling.
//
// `Vec` and other collections depend on this exemption for their default data
// pointer, so this test keeps the rule explicit rather than relying on zeroed C
// storage to produce the same value accidentally.
//
// `Slot<T>` is written out here rather than reached through `Vec`
// because the point is the DECLARATION FORM, and a test that goes
// through Vec would still pass if the exemption were replaced by a
// special case on `Vec` itself.

Slot*<T> = {
    data*:: Ptr<T> = null_ptr<T>(),
    len*:: usize = 3,
}

// Supplied explicitly, so the default is not what is read: a default is
// optional at construction, not mandatory.
filled = (p: Ptr<u8>) Slot<u8> { Slot<u8>(data: p, len: 1) }

main = (env: Env) Res<i32, AllocError> {
    empty = Slot<u8>();
    println("{}", empty.data.is_null());
    println("{}", empty.len);

    // a second element type: the default is emitted per instantiation,
    // and each one has to be spelled with ITS OWN pointee type
    wide = Slot<usize>();
    println("{}", wide.data.is_null());

    // the same field, supplied — a non-null pointer proves the field is
    // really read and `is_null` is really answering about it
    alloc ::= env.mem.alloc();
    room = alloc.raw(8, 8).try();
    println("{}", filled(room).data.is_null());
    Ok(0);
}
